  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 344 0 R
  /Alt (Two-by-two grid of four panels. Top-left (A, VAT Player Data): a heatmap of the reordered distance matrix showing three distinct dark-coloured square blocks along the diagonal, indicating three natural groups. Top-right (B, VAT Random Data): a similar heatmap for uniformly random data showing no block structure, with distances distributed evenly as a smooth gradient. Bottom-left (C, PCA Player Data): a two-dimensional scatter plot of the first two principal components with points coloured by cluster assignment, revealing three visually separable groups. Bottom-right (D, PCA Random Data): the same PCA projection for random data showing a single diffuse cloud with no discernible groupings.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
