860 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 859 0 R
  /Alt (Four-panel descriptive figure. Panel A shows two horizontal density curves with boxplots underneath: game-related SPANE balance scores concentrate on the positive side of the -6 to 6 scale with a long negative tail, and enjoyment concentrates near the top of its 1 to 7 scale. Panel B compares PvP (orange) and PvE (green) density curves for three performance metrics: kill/death ratios cluster around 1 in PvP but spread roughly an order of magnitude higher in PvE; hit accuracy peaks lower in PvP than in PvE; damage per second is likewise lower and narrower in PvP than in PvE. Panel C is a right-skewed histogram of total active hours over the 14-day window: most players played only a few hours, with a long tail of heavier players. Panel D is a timeline for one example participant with one row per day before the survey, showing coloured session segments by time of day and match type, mostly PvP Rush interleaved with Social Lobby visits in morning and mid-afternoon blocks; grey bands mark weekends, and a red dot on the final day marks the moment of survey completion, on a day without recorded play.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 1010 0 R
>>
